{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4067d9d1b20fea521fd18b3433949ebfaa095ce8053b54ff31649b524580e5a8","digest":{"component_or_area":"editor workflow server fixture","key_entities":["socket.getfqdn","ThreadingHTTPServer","HTTPServer.server_bind","TCPServer.server_bind","tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py","editor.py","editor_server.py","_LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer","127.0.0.1"],"problem_keywords":["reverse DNS","loopback server","HTTPServer construction","performance regression","socket.getfqdn"],"propositions":["CPython HTTPServer.server_bind calls socket.getfqdn for reverse DNS, consuming 35 seconds on GitHub macOS runners for numeric loopback address 127.0.0.1 during test fixture setup.","Editor workflow loopback server construction does not require or consume the reverse-resolved server_name value, making reverse DNS lookup contractually unnecessary.","A custom _LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer subclass delegates bind to TCPServer.server_bind and derives server_name from the literal bound address, eliminating reverse DNS while preserving all server behavior.","Test oracle verifies real loopback server starts without invoking socket.getfqdn, serves workflow endpoints, and handles shutdown while maintaining request handling and authentication coverage."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787416651864862001,"uuid":"85423baf-15aa-48f0-b438-5f46e253423c"}